  "limitations": [
    "This is independent source-followup research only, not a new scene or model stage. Two real source commits and all 30 original files are retained. All 11 earlier source-followup files are unchanged; 19 files extend the bounded evidence record under continued-screening/.",
    "The extension records eight corridor queries, thirteen birthday/holiday queries and ten follow-up queries, plus official-event screening. Producer records zero newly qualified multiview candidates. Negative results apply only to inspected scope, not proof that no other source or reuse exists.",
    "Nine official reservation/promotional thumbnails are 264x264; a 314x560 birthday poster is one character-occluded staircase view. Neither is a decoded native livestream frame or adequate multiview scene evidence. The derived contact image is a review aid, not an additional source viewpoint.",
    "Supported public content retrieval returned a login/navigation shell without image links; invalid canonical was not followed. Records distinguish technical insufficient content from explicit access denial. The archive worker does not repeat browsing, authentication, restricted-forum requests or any unavailable-content attempts.",
    "The original six selected source images and prior insufficient-view findings remain byte-for-byte preserved. The prior 98 successfully decoded images out of 103 collected URLs are not misreported as 103 successful downloads. New limited screening does not elevate old pink-tree/hotel sources to acceptance.",
    "The events observation originally called image 009 box-like content a recorder; that identity remains unverified and the expanded README explicitly restricts it to a box-like proxy. Backstage images/depth remain in their independent local-group archive and are not redefined as a complete room or second complete new scene.",
    "No BLEND/GLB or other model files are in this package. Archive worker verifies supplied bytes, producer manifests and true Git history; external source identity, scene acceptance and pixel interpretation are not independently researched here.",
    "This continues archive/source-followup-20261105 and history/source-followup-original-20261105, independent of the denied source-screening-increment receipt. That denied item stays paused with no retry or publication attempt.",
    "Normal Git fast-forward preserves the previous archive/receipt as versions/v0, all unrelated old paths and other remote refs. No modeling, rendering, production-tree edits, LFS, force pushes, credential copying, security changes, main writes, Issues or PRs. Temporary Library inputs remain for dot to manage."
  ],
